    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Incidence-Matrix Diagnostics\"\nauthor: \"Muhammad Yaseen\"\ndate: last-modified\nformat:\n  html:\n    self-contained: true\n    number-sections: true\n    toc: true\n    toc-depth: 3\n    highlight-style: github\n    code-fold: false\n    code-tools: true\n    html-math-method: mathjax\nvignette: >\n  %\\VignetteIndexEntry{Incidence-Matrix Diagnostics}\n  %\\VignetteEngine{quarto::html}\n  %\\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}\nexecute:\n  echo: true\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n---\n\n\n\n# Abstract\n\nThis vignette develops two matrix diagnostics that are useful across the whole\npackage:\n\n- pool overlap through $\\mathbf{M}\\mathbf{M}^\\top$\n- sample co-occurrence through $\\mathbf{M}^\\top\\mathbf{M}$\n\nThese diagnostics are presented as vignette material only. They are not new\nexported package helpers.\n\nThey also sit outside the constructor, decoder, simulation, and workflow APIs.\nThe matrices\n$\\mathbf{M}\\mathbf{M}^\\top$ and $\\mathbf{M}^\\top\\mathbf{M}$ are\ninterpretive summaries of a fixed design $\\mathbf{M}$; they do not choose a\ndecoder, execute retesting, or implement stage-2 protocol logic.\n\n# Architecture Boundary\n\nWithin the package layer model:\n\n1. construction returns $\\mathbf{M}$\n2. decoding interprets $\\mathbf{z}$ relative to $\\mathbf{M}$\n3. simulation generates $\\widetilde{\\mathbf{z}}$ and $\\mathbf{z}$\n4. workflow execution coordinates stage-1 and optional stage-2 logic\n5. reporting summarizes stored workflow objects\n\nThe diagnostics in this article belong to none of those execution layers. They\nare read-only summaries of a fixed incidence matrix.\n\n# Pool-Overlap Matrix\n\nFor $\\mathbf{M} \\in \\{0,1\\}^{J \\times N}$, the pool-overlap matrix is\n$\\mathbf{M}\\mathbf{M}^\\top = \\operatorname{tcrossprod}(\\mathbf{M})$.\n\nThe $(j, j')$ entry counts how many individuals belong to both\n$\\mathcal{P}_j$ and $\\mathcal{P}_{j'}$. The diagonal entries are the\npool sizes $n_j$.\n\nMore 